`LLMProvider`, `LLMModel`, `MCPServer` and `MCPTool` are gone, with their UI viewsets, REST endpoints, forms, filters, tables and menu items. All four are now the `nautobot-ai-models` models of the same purpose - `AIProvider`, `AIModel`, `MCPServer` and `MCPTool` - and this app reads them ([ADR 0010](../docs/decisions/0010-ai-registry-lives-in-nautobot-ai-models.md)). The REST routes `llm-providers`, `llm-models`, `mcp-servers` and `mcp-tools` move to `/api/plugins/ai-models/`; a client of any of the four needs its base URL changed.

Local MCP discovery goes with them: the `discovermcptools` management command, the per-server *Discover Tools* view and its route are deleted, and the AI Models app's **MCP Server Discovery** Job replaces all three. That app also ships a **Discover AI Models** Job, which reads `GET /v1/models` from an OpenAI-compatible provider and fills in its model catalogue - something this app never had.

Migration `0012` repoints `LLMUsageRecord.model`, `TicketEmbedding.model` and `AgentToolCall.tool` at the new tables and drops the four old ones. **No rows are copied.** This app has never been released, so there is no deployment whose registry would be lost; register the providers, models and servers again in the AI Models app, and run its two discovery Jobs.
